# PSR-5a — finance factory local production assert

## Gap (from PSR-5 inventory)

Nine dual-store factories call `assertProductionStorageDriver()` before choosing
memory vs prisma. `createFinanceRepository` only called `resolveStorageDriver()`,
relying solely on boot-time `assertProductionRuntimeIntegrity()`.

That is insufficient defense-in-depth: a composition root, script, or test that
constructs the finance singleton without full boot can still allocate
`InMemoryFinanceRepository` under a mis-set `STORAGE_DRIVER=memory` even when
production-grade integrity is expected later.

## Change

In `finance-repository.factory.ts`:

1. Import `assertProductionStorageDriver` alongside `resolveStorageDriver`.
2. Call `assertProductionStorageDriver()` at the start of
   `createFinanceRepository` (same posture as bookings/identity/drafts).

Behavior:

| Profile | Effect |
| --- | --- |
| test / development | unchanged — memory still allowed when driver resolves to memory |
| production / prodlike | throws `PRODUCTION_STORAGE_DRIVER_FORBIDDEN` if memory would be selected |

## Non-goals

- Removing the in-memory finance adapter
- Changing Prisma finance RLS
- Formal admin allowlist (PSR-5b)
- Tenant registry port (PSR-5c)

## Ratchet

```bash
node scripts/ops/psr-5-data-authority-inventory-smoke.mjs
node scripts/ops/psr-5a-finance-factory-assert-smoke.mjs
```

After land: `dual_store_missing_assert_count: 0` and
`finance_factory_missing_assert: false` in the PSR-5 inventory YAML.
